  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "A copy of a spell can be countered like any other spell, but it must be countered individually. Countering a spell with gravestorm won't affect the copies.",
      "oracle_id": "2d6a0d89-7ebd-420e-9892-be1506ab3714",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clue is an artifact type. Even though it appears on some cards with other permanent types, it's never a creature type, a land type, or anything but an artifact type.",
      "oracle_id": "2d6a0d89-7ebd-420e-9892-be1506ab3714",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gravestorm counts all permanents put into graveyards from the battlefield this turn. It doesn't matter who controlled those permanents, who owns them, or whether or not they were tokens.",
      "oracle_id": "2d6a0d89-7ebd-420e-9892-be1506ab3714",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect refers to a Clue, it means any Clue artifact, not just a Clue artifact token. For example, you can sacrifice Wrench to pay for Alquist Proft, Master Sleuth's activated ability.",
      "oracle_id": "2d6a0d89-7ebd-420e-9892-be1506ab3714",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some abilities trigger \"whenever you sacrifice a Clue\". Those abilities trigger whenever you sacrifice a Clue for any reason, not just to activate a Clue's activated ability.",
      "oracle_id": "2d6a0d89-7ebd-420e-9892-be1506ab3714",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some spells and abilities that investigate may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve. You won't create any Clue tokens.",
      "oracle_id": "2d6a0d89-7ebd-420e-9892-be1506ab3714",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The copies of Follow the Bodies created by its gravestorm ability are created on the stack, so they're not cast and won't cause abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell to trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "2d6a0d89-7ebd-420e-9892-be1506ab3714",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The triggered ability that creates the copies can itself be countered by anything that can counter a triggered ability. If it is countered, no copies will be put onto the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "2d6a0d89-7ebd-420e-9892-be1506ab3714",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't sacrifice a Clue to pay multiple costs. For example, you can't sacrifice a Clue token to activate its own ability and also to activate Alquist Proft, Master Sleuth's ability.",
      "oracle_id": "2d6a0d89-7ebd-420e-9892-be1506ab3714",
      "published_at": "2024-02-02",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A copy of a spell can be countered like any other spell, but it must be countered individually. Countering a spell with gravestorm won't affect the copies.",
      "oracle_id": "76bc6518-dea4-4a5c-a8a7-352cd297197b",
      "published_at": "2026-03-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gravestorm counts all permanents put into graveyards from the battlefield this turn. It doesn't matter who controlled those permanents, who owns them, or whether or not they were tokens.",
      "oracle_id": "76bc6518-dea4-4a5c-a8a7-352cd297197b",
      "published_at": "2026-03-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The copies of Ominous Harvest created by its gravestorm ability are created on the stack, so they're not cast and won't cause abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell to trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "76bc6518-dea4-4a5c-a8a7-352cd297197b",
      "published_at": "2026-03-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The triggered ability that creates the copies can itself be countered by anything that can counter a triggered ability. If it is countered, no copies will be put onto the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "76bc6518-dea4-4a5c-a8a7-352cd297197b",
      "published_at": "2026-03-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You may choose new targets for any of the copies. You can make different choices for each copy.",
      "oracle_id": "76bc6518-dea4-4a5c-a8a7-352cd297197b",
      "published_at": "2026-03-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Regenerating artifacts can regenerate from this.",
      "oracle_id": "84d32e68-72b9-432d-a023-7bc6a26b8ad0",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ]
}
